# VoLum UI

Read the smallest owner first:

- `VoLumControls.h`: umbrella only. Do not edit unless adding/removing includes.
- `VoLumTriptych.h`: `VoLumTriptychControl` (PRE/AMP/POST strip) and `VoLumChainConnectorControl`; umbrella for triptych pieces.
- `VoLumTriptychMotifs.h`: PITCH (double-helix) / COMP / PRE-NAM / DELAY / REVERB motifs used by pedal cards and Quiet slots.
- `VoLumTriptychMenus.h`: PRE capture menu (support-amp + custom pickers now use the shared `VoLumListMenuControl` in `VoLumCustomUi.h`).
- `VoLumPedalCardControl.h`: focused pedal cards with cached art layer and preset-name footer.
- `VoLumCoreControls.h`: sidebar, speaker row, knob row, meters, dividers/footers, channel stepper, keyboard hints, exact entry, param-value display, settings overlay frame.
- `VoLumHero.h`: procedural hero, AMP title strip, Dual Amp chip, lane PAN dots, support polarity control.
- `VoLumKeyboardModel.h`: shared keyboard target rings and per-parameter step sizes.
- `VoLumTunerMetronomeOverlay.h`: tuner and metronome controls.
- `VoLumTriptychState.h`: tiny shared enums.
- `VoLumColorHelpers.h`: shared colors and small drawing helpers, incl. the selection SSOT (`DrawVoLumSelection` / `SelectionInkColor` + `VoLumSelectionStyle`) and `DrawVoLumScrollbar`.
- `VoLumAmpList.h`: sidebar amp list control (rows, thumbnails, scrollbar drag). Pure scrollbar geometry lives in `VoLumAmpListScroll.h` (unit-tested in `test_volum_amp_list_scroll.cpp`).
- `VoLumCustomUi.h`: thin umbrella — just `#include`s the four custom-content control headers below. Include this; do not include the parts directly.
  - `VoLumPresetBar.h`: `VoLumPresetBarControl` (F5 preset strip).
  - `VoLumListMenu.h`: `VoLumListMenuControl` (reusable anchored dropdown).
  - `VoLumConfirmDialog.h`: `VoLumConfirmDialogControl` (destructive-delete modal).
  - `VoLumCustomOverlay.h`: `VoLumCustomOverlayControl` (full-window Manage CRUD + amp Builder). Still ~1480 lines but now self-contained; further internal carve is optional (it is one cohesive class, not a mixed-concern file).
- `VoLumCustomContentApi.h`: the index-based `volum::custom::*` session API the UI calls; a projection bridge over `GlobalContentStore()` (formerly `VoLumCustomContentMock.h` — production code, not a test mock).
- `VoLumCustomModel.h` / `VoLumContentStore.h`: pure custom-content manifest model + the registry-backed content store the bridge projects.
- `VoLumFractalArt.h`: large procedural art. Read only when changing fractals or hero/sidebar art.

Architecture:

- Layout is built in `NeuralAmpModeler::_BuildVoLumLayout(IGraphics*)`, defined in the tail-`#include`d `VoLumLayoutBuild.inc.cpp`. The constructor's `mLayoutFunc` lambda (~L505) just forwards to it. There is no `_AttachVoLumGraphics`; all controls are attached inside `_BuildVoLumLayout`. Because it is a member (not a captured lambda), it may only use members + its `pGraphics` arg, never constructor locals.
- `APP_API` means standalone; VST3-only behavior stays under `#ifndef APP_API`.
- Triptych has one expanded section at a time: PRE, AMP, or POST.
- Bottom knob row uses replace mode: section/pedal selection hides previous focused controls and shows new controls.
- PRE strip background is diagonal crosshatch; collapsed AMP strip is circuit-board grid.
- `NeuralAmpModeler.cpp` is the compiled translation unit; these are tail-`#include`d (or path-preserved) siblings, NOT independent build targets — a `#include` pastes the sibling at that exact point, so moving a member function into a sibling is behavior-neutral:
  - `VoLumProcessBlock.inc.cpp`, `VoLumLoader.inc.cpp`
  - `VoLumLayoutBuild.inc.cpp` (`_BuildVoLumLayout`, the full one-time attach pass)
  - `VoLumKeyboard.inc.cpp` (keyboard nav + exact entry), `VoLumLayoutRuntime.inc.cpp` (`_UpdateVoLumLayout`)
  - `VoLumSceneRig.inc.cpp` (channel/PRE-capture/custom-amp/IR rig helpers), `VoLumAmpMenus.inc.cpp` (factory reset + preset/support menus + dual-amp focus)
  - `VoLumSettings.inc.cpp` is itself a thin umbrella that tail-includes `VoLumSettingsLocks.inc.cpp` (save-to-slot/lock/dirty/snapshots), `VoLumSettingsScene.inc.cpp` (restore/apply/DSP caches/file I/O/lite), and `VoLumSettingsPresets.inc.cpp` (preset bank)
  - `Unserialization.cpp`
- Source-string regression locks in `test_volum_ui_regressions.cpp` use `ReadPluginSource()` over `NeuralAmpModeler.cpp` plus the tail-included `.inc.cpp` siblings. Moving a function between those files does not break a lock unless the string itself changes.
- Promoting `.inc.cpp` siblings to real separate translation units is a 1.1 hygiene follow-up that needs macOS verification.
- Any list/menu that can grow at runtime (presets, IRs, pedals, custom amps, custom-amp file manifest, support-amp picker) MUST clip drawing to its rect, cap its height to the window, and provide a scrollbar + mouse-wheel/trackpad scrolling. See `VoLumListMenuControl`, `VoLumPreCaptureMenuControl`, and the builder file list in `VoLumCustomUi.h` for the pattern. Do not add an unbounded list that draws past its rect. Draw the scrollbar with `DrawVoLumScrollbar` so every list reads identically.

Selection language (SSOT — every mutually-exclusive control):

- A control that shows one selected/active item out of a group MUST draw its
  selected/hover background via `DrawVoLumSelection(g, rect, active, hovered, style)`
  and tint its label via `SelectionInkColor(style, active)` (both in
  `VoLumColorHelpers.h`). Do NOT hand-draw an ad-hoc fill/border/glow — that is
  how new pickers historically shipped with a missing or mismatched highlight.
- Pick the `VoLumSelectionStyle` that matches the surface: `AmberPicker` for
  mode pickers / sub-pills (`VoLumModePickerControl`, `VoLumSubModePillControl`),
  `Brass` for the cab/speaker row and metronome time-sigs, `ListTeal` for sidebar
  /list-menu rows. Keep the dialect; do not invent a new one.
- `test_volum_ui_regressions.cpp` has a source-guard pin asserting the mode
  pickers route through `DrawVoLumSelection`; extend it when you add a picker.

Screenshot harness for runtime-only states:

- The sidebar custom-amp list (scrollbar overflow, custom thumbnails) is empty in
  a fresh sandbox. To capture it deterministically, launch the app with
  `VOLUM_SEED_CUSTOM_AMPS=N` (debug builds only; compiled out of Release). It
  redirects the content store to a temp sandbox and seeds N custom amps, so
  `win-screenshot.ps1` can capture overflow without touching the user's real
  content store.

Verification:

- UI/layout change: run the Windows app smoke check (`AGENTS.md` "Fast Commands") and inspect the app.
- If params/keyboard behavior changed too, also run the Windows tests.
- Prefer pure helper tests for layout/state before source-string locks:
  - Triptych geometry belongs in `VoLumTriptychLayout.h` / `test_volum_ui_regressions.cpp`.
  - PRE capture discovery belongs in `VoLumPrePedalCaptures.h` / `test_volum_pre_pedal_captures.cpp`.
  - Signal-chain visibility/enablement decisions belong in `VoLumProcessingPlan.h` / `test_volum_processing_plan.cpp`.
  - Sidebar list scrollbar geometry belongs in `VoLumAmpListScroll.h` / `test_volum_amp_list_scroll.cpp`.
- Never dump new controls into the `VoLumControls.h` umbrella; keep ownership in
  the file that owns the surface.
